{"hash": "05b9592f03fb3910", "text": "Now the drawer that matters most. At the root of many projects sits a file called dot E N V. Inside are plain lines: a name, an equals sign, and a value, usually a key or a password. When your program starts, if it's set up to look for this file, it loads those lines as environment variables. That drawer has no lock. It's plain text. Hidden means out of sight, not encrypted. Rule one: it never goes into git. Put it on the git ignore list before your first commit. Adding it later doesn't pull it out of the history, and once a key has leaked, the only real fix is to replace it. Rule two: never paste it into a chat, and never let an agent read it. Claude Code's own documentation says that anything a tool reads, a key included, ends up in a transcript file in another hidden folder. GitHub now blocks some known kinds of key from reaching public repositories, but only the kinds it recognises, and you can override it. It's a net, not a plan.", "alignment": {"characters": ["N", "o", "w", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "r", "a", "w", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "m", "a", "t", "t", "e", "r", "s", " ", "m", "o", "s", "t", ".", " ", "A", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "r", "o", "o", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "m", "a", "n", "y", " ", "p", "r", "o", "j", "e", "c", "t", "s", " ", "s", "i", "t", "s", " ", "a", " ", "f", "i", "l", "e", " ", "c", "a", "l", "l", "e", "d", " ", "d", "o", "t", " ", "E", " ", "N", " ", "V", ".", " ", "I", "n", "s", "i", "d", "e", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "p", "l", "a", "i", "n", " ", "l", "i", "n", "e", "s", ":", " ", "a", " ", "n", "a", "m", "e", ",", " ", "a", "n", " ", "e", "q", "u", "a", "l", "s", " ", "s", "i", "g", "n", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "a", " ", "v", "a", "l", "u", "e", ",", " ", "u", "s", "u", "a", "l", "l", "y", " ", "a", " ", "k", "e", "y", " ", "o", "r", " ", "a", " ", "p", "a", "s", "s", "w", "o", "r", "d", ".", " ", "W", "h", "e", "n", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "p", "r", "o", "g